{
  "summary": "P1 lost laptop (KB-021). User Mei Chen (user_id 9, Operations, Logistics Analyst) reports she likely left her work laptop in an Uber last night; she does not know whether it was locked. Device: BL-LT-0109, macOS 15, assigned to her. Status: ONLINE, last check-in 2026-10-11T02:40:48Z (~21:40 Chicago, last night), no warnings. Sign-in logs (14 days): all successful, Chicago only, corporate/residential networks, Duo push, no failures, no hosting networks, no sign-ins since 2026-10-09; no sign of misuse yet. Account active, VPN enabled. Action taken: block_sign_in queued for technician approval. Needed: remote lock/wipe of BL-LT-0109 while it is online; confirm block approval; password reset once user identity verified by callback. Data on device: Operations/logistics analyst work files, cached M365 mail (mailbox ~50 GB, 99% full), VPN profile. User asked for time/place last seen and to contact Uber / file police report if not recovered.",
  "reason": "KB-021 requires escalation always for remote lock/wipe; P1."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, thanks for telling us so quickly. We're treating this as urgent. Your laptop was last connected to our systems last night, and so far we see no sign-ins to your account from anyone else. To be safe, we've asked a technician to block sign-ins to your account and VPN so nobody can use a saved session on the laptop. Once they approve it, you won't be able to sign in for a while. We've also sent the case to our senior team so they can lock or wipe the laptop remotely. After that, we'll check your identity by phone and help you set a new password. Please reply with roughly when and where you last had the laptop (the time and route of the ride). Please also report it to Uber through the app's lost item feature. If it isn't recovered, or you think it was stolen, please file a police report. If you notice anything unusual on your account in the meantime, let us know right away.",
  "internal_note": "P1 lost laptop, following KB-021. User: Mei Chen, user_id 9. Device BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15) shows online, last check-in 2026-10-11T02:40:48Z (about 21:40 Chicago). Sign-in logs: 10 successful sign-ins over 14 days, all from Chicago on corporate or residential networks with Duo push. No failed attempts, no hosting networks, nothing after 2026-10-09. Lock state unknown, so I queued block_sign_in (approval_id 1, pending). Escalated to Tier 2 for remote lock/wipe (escalation_id 1). Still to do: approve the block, lock or wipe the laptop while it's online, and reset her password after verifying her by callback. Asked the user when and where she last saw it, and to contact Uber and file a police report if needed. Side note: her mailbox is 99.4% full.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-021"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
